4. ADVISORY (not blocking; no round-2 obligation unless the fix is free)
=============================================================================

A1 — apps/web/tests-serve/board.spec.ts:516-518's comment credits the pending human
     gate to "W-003's human 'patron' gate". Measured: W-003's pending gate is `qa`
     (kind: agent); the human `patron` gate is pending on W-004
     (examples/sample-studio/opera/W-004.md). The assertion is right, the comment
     names the wrong opus — and a future builder narrowing the fixture on that comment
     would break behaviour 9 silently.

A2 — packages/cli/src/containment.test.ts:261-271 (+10 lines) is outside Files owned
     and was not disclosed. It is mechanically forced (the pinned-call registry
     requires a disposition for board.spec.ts's two new path joins) and both entries
     carry a real why. Accepted as bookkeeping the suite demands, but it belonged in
     the disclosure list — the same paragraph that carried Seats.tsx and w025.css.

A3 — apps/web/test/boardview.test.ts:204 finds the api.js import line with
     Array.find(), so a SECOND runtime import line from ../api.js would never be
     examined. The brief's wording is "No other runtime import from that module"
     (*Board.tsx*). One extra .filter().length === 1 closes it.

A4 — apps/web/tests-serve/board.spec.ts:146 does not await page.route(). It is
     effective in practice (M16 proves a write on mount is caught, so the route is
     live before navigation), but TARGET-9's requirement is an ordering one and it is
     currently relying on Playwright's channel ordering rather than saying so.

A5 — FOR THE ARCHITECT, NOT THE BUILDER: on the Patron's own officina the needs-you
     column can never fill. studio/bisellium.yml:23-28 declares tests/lint/types
     (automated) and spec/review (agent) — no probatio of kind: human anywhere — and
     humanGateIds filters on kind === "human" (board.ts:66-68). Measured on the real
     studio: "SMOKE needs_you rendered count: 0", drawer banner "absent" on every card.
     So DIRECTION §6's pinned attention column, the needs-you banner, the petitio join
     and W-073's whole reason to exist are all dead on the only officina that matters,
     while being exactly what the brief specifies. The implementation is conformant;
     the contract is pointed at a gate kind this studio does not use. This wants a
     Patron/architect answer (declare a human probatio, or widen needs-you to a pending
     AGENT gate awaiting the Patron), not a builder fix, and it is the single largest
     product gap in the opus.

=============================================================================
5. VERDICT
=============================================================================

FAIL, round 1. Eight blocking findings: two live bugs measured on real data (B1, B2),
four prescribed mutations that survive (B3, B4, B5, B6), one specified surface that is
absent (B7), one specified seam that is not wired (B8). The reds are genuine, the
read-only decree is genuinely measured on both halves, the server read surface is
sound, and the folded-in TTL knob delivered its 5.13s.

Two of the eight are one shape, and a round-2 fix should treat them as such: an
assertion that its own implementation satisfies by accident (B1's Esc focus, which
never leaves the card; B2's phone column, which is the default scroll position). Both
were found by moving the state the test never moves.

The red-provenance disclosure (D1) is not among the blocking eight, but it has fired
D-024's second kill arm and is not waivable by the censor. That is the Patron's call
and P-012's cue.

-- qa-lead (censor), via Claude Opus 5
